{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-315e-7795-bf42-6792deab3507","id":"01a1a5ba-a891-7389-92f4-817ca4ebdbf7","idempotency_key":"d265d64bf5a12d65c9c6fc12f42a49dbd428664bcb61588714064ef520d8564c","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T08:43:55Z","payload":{"note":"Approval UI complete. Panel: pending writes listed with tool, summary and the changeset's diff; per-row approve/deny, approve-all, and the outcome shown in place ('applied · played e4'). Auto-approve scopes: a 'Never ask for:' row with board-write / study-content / destructive, read from the session and saved through the new PUT /api/ai/sessions/{id}/permissions, which refuses an unknown scope name rather than storing it. The queue records a real preview for moves (BoardContent::with_move uses the same validation as play_move), so a row reads 'moves 0 -> 1 (e4)'. Approving replays the reviewed call through BoardWriteHost with the stored arguments; a refused write leaves the decision standing and reports why. Evidence: cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown passes; cdp_ai_approvals.js -> AI_APPROVALS_PASS on a clean database (one pending play_move with its diff, approve answers applied · played e4, board reaches revision 2 with {\"moves\":[\"e4\"]}); cdp_ai_scopes.js -> AI_SCOPES_PASS (granting board-write stores {\"in_app\":[\"board-write\"],\"mcp\":[]}, the next play writes straight through, no pending approval, board at revision 2). NOT built: per-row selection for bulk approve; mcp scopes are accepted by the route but the panel only edits in-app.","target":"t-4bfb"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
